---
title: Hooks API
description: Reference for frame, runtime, pointer, texture, and advanced user-context hooks.
---

All hooks come from `/svelte`, `/react`, or `/vue`; advanced user-context functions come from the matching `/advanced` entrypoint. Runtime hooks require a `FragCanvas` ancestor.

## `useFrame`

```ts
useFrame(callback, options?): UseFrameResult
useFrame(key, callback, options?): UseFrameResult
```

| `UseFrameOptions` | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `autoStart` | `boolean` | `true` |
| `autoInvalidate` | `boolean` | `true` |
| `invalidation` | `FrameTaskInvalidation` | Implicit |
| `stage` | `FrameKey &#124; FrameStage` | Main stage |
| `before`, `after` | Task reference or array | — |
| `running` | `() => boolean` | — |

`UseFrameResult` contains `task: { key, stage }`, `start()`, `stop()`, and `started: Subscribable<boolean>`.

### `FrameState`

| Member | Type |
| --- | --- |
| `time`, `delta` | `number` |
| `canvas` | `HTMLCanvasElement` |
| `renderMode` | `RenderMode` |
| `autoRender` | `boolean` |
| `setUniform` | `(name, value) => void` |
| `setTexture` | `(name, value) => void` |
| `writeStorageBuffer` | `(name, data, { offset? }?) => void` |
| `readStorageBuffer` | `(name) => Promise<ArrayBuffer>` |
| `invalidate` | `(token?) => void` |
| `advance` | `() => void` |

Storage writes require a four-byte-aligned offset and byte length and must fit in the declared buffer. The runtime copies the bytes immediately. Reading a buffer flushes its queued writes in call order before readback.

## `useMotionGPU`

Returns `MotionGPUContext`:

| Member | Type |
| --- | --- |
| `canvas` | `HTMLCanvasElement &#124; undefined` |
| `size` | `CurrentReadable<{ width; height }>` in CSS pixels |
| `dpr`, `maxDelta` | `CurrentWritable<number>` |
| `renderMode` | `CurrentWritable<RenderMode>` |
| `autoRender` | `CurrentWritable<boolean>` |
| `user` | `CurrentWritable<Record<string &#124; symbol, unknown>>` |
| `invalidate`, `advance` | `() => void` |
| `scheduler` | `MotionGPUScheduler` |

The scheduler exposes `createStage`, `getStage`, schedule inspection, diagnostics/profiling setters and getters, reset, last-run timings, and rolling snapshots.

## `usePointer(options?)`

| Option | Default |
| --- | --- |
| `enabled` | `true` |
| `requestFrame` | `'auto'` |
| `capturePointer` | `true` |
| `trackWhilePressedOutsideCanvas` | `true` |
| `clickEnabled` | `true` |
| `clickMaxDurationMs` | `350` |
| `clickMaxMovePx` | `8` |
| `clickButtons` | `[0]` |
| `onMove`, `onDown`, `onUp`, `onClick` | — |

`requestFrame` accepts `'auto'`, `'invalidate'`, `'advance'`, or `'none'`. Auto resolves to advance in manual mode, invalidate in on-demand mode, and none in always mode.

The result contains `state: CurrentReadable<PointerState>`, `lastClick: CurrentReadable<PointerClick | null>`, and `resetClick()`. State includes `px`, `uv`, `ndc`, inside/pressed/dragging state, pointer identity and buttons, down position, deltas, and velocities.

React applies a new options object on each render. In Svelte and Vue, pass `() => options` when `enabled`, outside tracking, callbacks, or other settings can change; the hook updates listeners without remounting.

## `useTexture(urlInput, options?)`

`urlInput` is `string[] | (() => string[])`. Svelte and Vue options may also be lazy; React options are an object.

| Result | Type |
| --- | --- |
| `textures` | `CurrentReadable<LoadedTexture[] &#124; null>` |
| `loading` | `CurrentReadable<boolean>` |
| `error` | `CurrentReadable<Error &#124; null>` |
| `errorReport` | `CurrentReadable<MotionGPUErrorReport &#124; null>` |
| `reload` | `() => Promise<void>` |

`TextureLoadOptions` contains `colorSpace`, `requestInit`, `decode`, `signal`, `update`, `flipY`, `premultipliedAlpha`, and `generateMipmaps`.

## Advanced user context

```ts
useMotionGPUUserContext(): CurrentReadable<Record<string | symbol, unknown>>
useMotionGPUUserContext<T>(namespace): CurrentReadable<T | undefined>
setMotionGPUUserContext(namespace, valueOrFactory, options?): T | undefined
```

React also provides a context-bound `useSetMotionGPUUserContext()` setter.

| Option | Values | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `existing` | `'skip' &#124; 'replace' &#124; 'merge'` | `'skip'` |
| `functionValue` | `'factory' &#124; 'value'` | `'factory'` |

See [Frame Scheduler](/docs/frame-scheduler), [Hooks & Context](/docs/hooks-and-context), [Texture Loading](/docs/texture-loading), and [User Context](/docs/user-context).
